SUMMONING CONTRACT — REGISTRY ENTRY
Konohagakure Fuinjutsu Archive

A summoning contract binds a shinobi to a clan of summon creatures.
The contract is signed in the summoner's blood and stored in the
restricted archive. Only registered signatories may summon.

Registered Contracts of Note:
- Toad Contract (Mount Myoboku): historically held by the Fourth
  Hokage, Minato Namikaze, and the Sannin Jiraiya. Current apprentice
  signatory: Naruto Uzumaki.
- Slug Contract (Katsuyu): held by the Godaime Hokage, Tsunade.
- Ninken (Hound) Contract: held by Kakashi Hatake — Pakkun and pack.
- Snake Contract: FLAGGED — associated with the defector Orochimaru.
  Signatory rights revoked; entry retained for intelligence only.

Procedure: To sign, apply blood to the fingertips, mark the scroll,
and complete the summoning hand seals (Boar, Dog, Bird, Monkey, Ram).
All new contracts must be witnessed and logged by an archive keeper.
